Whisper: the product version in Windows file details is Whisper's

What: config/create_rc.py writes the display version (MOZ_APP_VERSION_DISPLAY) as the
product version string of every Windows program and library, instead of Firefox's
version (browser/app/module.ver and ipc/app/module.ver ask for MOZ_APP_VERSION).
prepare.sh makes the display version Whisper's own (WHISPER_VERSION in
gecko/release.env, through configure's --with-version-file-path), while the
application version stays Firefox's.
Why: Explorer's Properties > Details showed "Product name: Whisper" with "Product
version: 159.0.1", Firefox's number; it should say Whisper's version. The file
version and the numeric version resource stay Firefox's.
---
--- a/config/create_rc.py
+++ b/config/create_rc.py
@@ -304,7 +304,10 @@
         company=buildconfig.substs.get("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", ""),
         description=overrides.get("WIN32_MODULE_DESCRIPTION", ""),
         mfversion=overrides.get("WIN32_MODULE_FILEVERSION_STRING", milestone_string),
-        mpversion=overrides.get("WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION_STRING", milestone_string),
+        # Whisper: the product version of every program and library is Whisper's own
+        # (the display version, which prepare.sh sets from release.env), also where a
+        # module.ver asks for MOZ_APP_VERSION; the file version stays Firefox's.
+        mpversion=app_version_display or milestone_string,
         module=overrides.get("WIN32_MODULE_NAME", ""),
         trademarks="",
         binary=overrides.get("WIN32_MODULE_ORIGINAL_FILENAME", binary),
